Text:
fearlessMessage is a program that sends one Message to the single manager, and prints the Answer of the single manager on the standard output of fearlessMessage.
The single manager is 'reachable at Port' when the ManagerFolder at the 'manager path' holds the LockFile "single_manager_at_" Port ".lock", and a process holds the lock of that LockFile.
The single manager is 'not reachable' when no Port makes the single manager reachable at that Port.
The 'name' of a folder is ProjectName when ProjectName ".fearless" is the only file at top level in that folder ending with ".fearless".

Grammar:
Message ::= "EditMetadata " Base16                                     \
          | "EditMetadata " Info                                       \
          | "Register " Base16                                         \
          | "Forget " Target                                           \
          | "Forget " Base16                                           \
          | "Kind " Target " " Kind                                    \
          | "Mount " Target " " TypeName " " Target'                   \
          | "Unmount " Target " " TypeName                             \
          | "Attenuate " Target " " TypeName " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen  \
          | "SelectMains " Target " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen             \
          | "Quit"
Target ::= "Name(" ProjectName ")" | "Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")"
Base16 ::= "Base16:" ([0-9A-F][0-9A-F])+
Answer ::= "Applied\n" | "Refused\n" Error
Error ::= ...
AnyText ::= any sequence of characters

Well formedness:
in Base16: Base16 encodes a valid OS FS path

Define fearlessMessage$send(Message,Port):
A action fearlessMessage connects to Port on the loopback address, and sends Message on the connection
B action fearlessMessage prints on the standard output of fearlessMessage the text arriving on the connection, as the text arrives
C fact The connection is closed.
D action fearlessMessage ends

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with the one argument Message.
B fact The single manager is reachable at Port.
C action fearlessMessage$send(Message,Port)

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with the one argument Message.
B fact The single manager is not reachable.
C action fearlessMessage runs fearlessManager, and waits until the single manager is reachable or one minute has passed
D after The single manager is reachable at Port.
E action fearlessMessage$send(Message,Port)

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with the one argument Message.
B fact The single manager is not reachable.
C action fearlessMessage runs fearlessManager, and waits until the single manager is reachable or one minute has passed
D after The single manager is not reachable.
E action fearlessMessage prints internalErrorManagerNotStarted() on the standard error of fearlessMessage, and ends

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with the arguments AnyText1 .. AnyTextn.
B fact n is not 1, or AnyText1 is not of form Message.
C action fearlessMessage prints messageErrorArgumentsAreNotOneMessage(AnyText1 .. AnyTextn) on the standard error of fearlessMessage, and ends

Implementation notes:
A shell splits the text of a call into arguments, and a Message holds spaces, so a caller writes the Message between double quotes: fearlessMessage "Quit" and fearlessMessage "Register Base16:432F61" are calls with the one argument Message.
A Message of form "EditMetadata " Info can hold double quotes. Written between double quotes with no escape, as in fearlessMessage "EditMetadata Infos.list(Infos.map("path", ..))", the text is cut by the shell at each double quote: fearlessMessage gets more than one argument, or one argument that is not of form Message, and fearlessMessage prints messageErrorArgumentsAreNotOneMessage.
fearlessMessage sends Message on the connection with no double quotes around Message, and fearlessManager$delegate returns a Message to fearlessManager.queue with no shell in between: fearlessManager handles a Message of form "EditMetadata " Info with any Info.
